  <title>Set up your first backup</title>
  <desc>Choose where backups go, what to copy, and save your recovery key.</desc>

  <p>The first time you open Delta it says <gui>Backups are not set up</gui>. Choose <gui style="button">Set up backups</gui>.
  The assistant has a few short pages, with <gui style="button">Next</gui> and <gui style="button">Back</gui>.
  Nothing is created until you choose <gui style="button">Create backups</gui> on the last one.</p>

  <steps>
    <item>
      <title>Where should backups go?</title>
      <p>Pick a <gui>Folder</gui> with <gui style="button">Choose…</gui>, which must be new or empty, or one of the
      connected drives. On a drive, backups go in a folder called <file>delta-backups</file>. Delta tells you at once if
      the place is not usable: a path that does not exist, a file, a whole disk, or a folder that is not empty.</p>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>What should be backed up?</title>
      <p>By default, <gui>Everything in your home folder</gui>. To choose, add folders with
      <gui style="button">Choose a folder to back up</gui>.</p>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Save your recovery key</title>
      <p>Backups are encrypted. Use <gui style="button">Save to a file…</gui> and keep the file somewhere safe,
      <em>away from this computer</em>. You cannot finish until you turn on <gui>I have saved my recovery key</gui>.
      <gui style="button">Copy</gui> alone does not count as saving it. If you prefer your own passphrase, turn on
      <gui>Use my own passphrase instead</gui>.</p>
      <p>See <link xref="recovery-key"/>.</p>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Create the backups</title>
      <p>Choose <gui style="button">Create backups</gui>. Delta prepares the destination and starts protecting your files.</p>
    </item>
  </steps>

  <section id="existing">
    <title>Use a backup you already have</title>
    <p>If the folder already holds a Delta backup, for example after reinstalling, the assistant offers
    <gui>Use the existing repository</gui>. Enter its passphrase and choose
    <gui style="button">Use this repository</gui>. Nothing in it is erased.</p>
  </section>
</page>
